            <ArticleTitle>Application of optical coherence tomography in the treatment of coronary bifurcation lesions.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E39-42</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Optical coherence tomography (OCT) is a novel intravascular imaging modality with excellent resolution. We report the application of OCT in 3 coronary bifurcation interventions, in which OCT allowed optimization of the final procedural result, by detecting a dissection, intracoronary thrombus and by confirming complete ostial coverage by a stent.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
